{"title":"2014 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 24","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_3_(Ptolemy&#39;s_but_Quicker)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3 (Ptolemy's but Quicker)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Solution_4\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 4</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#See_also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_24&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/1/3/f13a96240c51d61ba3733d9f5c3020fa92ec4136.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABCDE$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"74\" height=\"14\" /> be a pentagon inscribed in a circle such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/9/0/d906d862c3dd087eaf46ce688835c0ac904fa017.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB = CD = 3$\" width=\"115\" height=\"13\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/2/4/82476ee1ecb0789b759563fb87ce38e05ad2591c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC = DE = 10$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"125\" height=\"13\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/b/3/2b3ea3420065676e96be28a218009582eb4aad7f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AE= 14$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"70\" height=\"13\" />.  The sum of the lengths of all diagonals of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/1/3/f13a96240c51d61ba3733d9f5c3020fa92ec4136.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABCDE$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"74\" height=\"14\" /> is equal to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/7/f/27f583697295fc6f723862c13228ee55107c33ca.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{m}{n}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"22\" height=\"34\" />, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f5047d1e0cbb50ec208923a22cd517c55100fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> are relatively prime positive integers.  What is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/2/d/02dbab3601fa6cce490d54263017048f69e1a35d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m+n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"51\" height=\"14\" />&#160;?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/a/0/1a068c190ce71c069c27dea953d68f7fc798da31.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A) }129\\qquad \\textbf{(B) }247\\qquad \\textbf{(C) }353\\qquad \\textbf{(D) }391\\qquad \\textbf{(E) }421\\qquad$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"443\" height=\"17\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_24&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/5/1/351e1240e130881286563af162324e632aa58dae.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BE=a$\" width=\"63\" height=\"12\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/7/d/07daaeb34175de9e89ff0ceb2668cfd950c92814.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AD=b$\" width=\"61\" height=\"13\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/8/b/38b0c12ae07e96772016f7011e1ce8f31e1f3212.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AC=CE=BD=c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"169\" height=\"14\" />. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/0/5/a055f405829e64a3b70253ab67cb45ed6ed5bb29.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$F$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> be on <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/a/6/9a65c05bd85d2609bea5db2b109ed5f556463511.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AE$\" width=\"27\" height=\"13\" /> such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/a/b/7abd03688fcffe5854ddb38c602c3dc51e6205da.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CF \\perp AE$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"83\" height=\"14\" />. \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/3/0/f309928844b6dc47e0410382e86dd44b9cf39966.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] size(200); defaultpen(linewidth(0.4)+fontsize(10)); pen s = linewidth(0.8)+fontsize(8);  pair O,A,B,C,D,E0,F; O=origin; A= dir(198); path c = CR(O,1); real r = 0.13535; B = IP(c, CR(A,3*r)); C = IP(c, CR(B,10*r)); D = IP(c, CR(C,3*r)); E0 = OP(c, CR(D,10*r)); F = foot(C,A,E0);  dot(&quot;$A$&quot;, A, A-O); dot(&quot;$B$&quot;, B, B-O); dot(&quot;$C$&quot;, C, C-O); dot(&quot;$D$&quot;, D, D-O); dot(&quot;$E$&quot;, E0, E0-O); dot(&quot;$F$&quot;, F, F-C); label(&quot;$c$&quot;,A--C,S); label(&quot;$c$&quot;,E0--C,W); label(&quot;$7$&quot;,F--E0,S); label(&quot;$7$&quot;,F--A,S); label(&quot;$3$&quot;,A--B,2*W); label(&quot;$10$&quot;,B--C,2*N); label(&quot;$3$&quot;,C--D,2*NE); label(&quot;$10$&quot;,D--E0,E); draw(A--B--C--D--E0--A, black+0.8);  draw(CR(O,1), s); draw(A--C--E0, royalblue); draw(C--F, royalblue+dashed); draw(rightanglemark(E0,F,C,2)); MA(&quot;\\theta&quot;,A,B,C,0.075); MA(&quot;\\pi-\\theta&quot;,C,E0,A,0.1); [/asy]\" width=\"335\" height=\"322\" />\nIn <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/0/3/803aa1ba74919a869eee5f679bb42af62b79d343.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle CFE$\" width=\"58\" height=\"13\" /> we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/2/2/522f0bfeedb7e479c59c2e69e68e564e2e8891ac.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\cos\\theta = -\\cos(\\pi-\\theta)=-7/c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"225\" height=\"20\" />. We use the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Law_of_Cosines\" title=\"Law of Cosines\">Law of Cosines</a> on <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c3a2d2224f7d163b46d702132425d47828bf538.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"61\" height=\"18\" /> to get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/8/8/488722039f414fdb9ec301eade66d2db865d8334.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$60\\cos\\theta = 109-c^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"149\" height=\"18\" />.  Eliminating <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/e/5/de5a3b34841a0696e4e3afc4fda90bda98eead51.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\cos\\theta$\" width=\"36\" height=\"13\" /> we get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/7/7/977e97316d799f8628b9f4247b4a85d82fa07934.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c^3-109c-420=0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"157\" height=\"18\" /> which factorizes as \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/2/1/a2176254a587b20b97e42f6aea2f74ad3256151d.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[(c+7)(c+5)(c-12)=0.\\]\" width=\"204\" height=\"18\" />Discarding the negative roots we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/9/9/49986ad1ae5d88da95d611165eb5055d9ffcaa25.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c=12$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"49\" height=\"12\" />. Thus <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/5/0/9504774d8e2ae2ddbb44cb3054935cc072cc91d5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BD=AC=CE=12$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"180\" height=\"14\" />. For <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/5/1/351e1240e130881286563af162324e632aa58dae.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BE=a$\" width=\"63\" height=\"12\" />, we use Ptolemy's theorem on cyclic quadrilateral <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/4/9/249aa48167a0ec4808fb235a2796eaffab883dba.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABCE$\" width=\"56\" height=\"13\" /> to get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/d/e/1dec32fac350cbdda4d9085a6794e62fdc318584.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a=44/3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"72\" height=\"20\" />. For <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/7/d/07daaeb34175de9e89ff0ceb2668cfd950c92814.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AD=b$\" width=\"61\" height=\"13\" />, we use <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Ptolemy%27s_theorem\" title=\"Ptolemy&#39;s theorem\">Ptolemy's theorem</a> on cyclic quadrilateral <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/0/8/208eeb07928a5d764be9ca1d81d7a3f275308c65.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ACDE$\" width=\"57\" height=\"13\" /> to get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/7/9/8791c0dc8cd1875ea051cf653bd30eefc9c6c5fd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b=27/2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"70\" height=\"20\" />.\n</p><p>The sum of the lengths of the diagonals is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/4/e/04e9037395e8a9efa420e421ccbd48934620a347.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$12+12+12+\\tfrac{44}{3}+\\tfrac{27}{2} = \\tfrac{385}{6}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -7px\" width=\"228\" height=\"23\" /> so the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/4/d/b4de474c629d79eb01852c02dce57d26958f78d9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$385 + 6 = \\fbox{\\textbf{(D) }391}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"155\" height=\"28\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_24&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> denote the length of a diagonal opposite adjacent sides of length <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/2/0/820a20de2847dfdc1bc5cffc8d904933150032bd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$14$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" /> for sides <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/2/0/820a20de2847dfdc1bc5cffc8d904933150032bd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$14$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/6/fc606f7f1e530731ab4f1cc364c01dc64a4455ee.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/7/3372c1cb6d68cf97c2d231acc0b47b95a9ed04cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" /> for sides <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/6/fc606f7f1e530731ab4f1cc364c01dc64a4455ee.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />. Using Ptolemy's Theorem on the five possible quadrilaterals in the configuration, we obtain:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/9/6/1962458e45bc6dba8792d87cf96a526ea760b73a.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align} c^2 &amp;= 3a+100 \\\\ c^2 &amp;= 10b+9 \\\\ ab &amp;= 30+14c \\\\ ac &amp;= 3c+140\\\\ bc &amp;= 10c+42 \\end{align}\" width=\"293\" height=\"121\" />\n</p><p>Using equations <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/d/9/0d9c3b1c142cbd3f8217dabc160c57e4750df241.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"21\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/2/f/62f62a19f0425d8e6121ca0c1cfd3ce96e43c9c5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(2)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"21\" height=\"18\" />, we obtain:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/1741a7cb15672aabf8a9e28c5bd6ad4011ac0bff.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[a = \\frac{c^2-100}{3}\\]\" width=\"100\" height=\"39\" />\n</p><p>and\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/7/8/b782ca88db9a5997d8183e2c6b3f53c3fd3648c7.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[b = \\frac{c^2-9}{10}\\]\" width=\"80\" height=\"39\" />\n</p><p>Plugging into equation <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/0/4/104992efa4deaa9a2dfeeec9b331ad0bf628f80a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(4)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"25\" height=\"20\" />, we find that:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/5/f/85f84185bc8b0b957894a51615d721e9a6af412c.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*} \\frac{c^2-100}{3}c &amp;= 3c + 140\\\\ \\frac{c^3-100c}{3} &amp;= 3c + 140\\\\ c^3-100c &amp;= 9c + 420\\\\ c^3-109c-420 &amp;=0\\\\ (c-12)(c+7)(c+5)&amp;=0 \\end{align*}\" width=\"257\" height=\"163\" />\n</p><p>Or similarly into equation <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/3/7/737a366a904e00f936f8728869ad8f2587dab46f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(5)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"21\" height=\"18\" /> to check:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/5/5/a553be1ff95228fed2fbed507af968a2583d341d.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*} \\frac{c^2-9}{10}c &amp;= 10c+42\\\\ \\frac{c^3-9c}{10} &amp;= 10c + 42\\\\ c^3-9c &amp;= 100c + 420\\\\ c^3-109c-420 &amp;=0\\\\ (c-12)(c+7)(c+5)&amp;=0 \\end{align*}\" width=\"275\" height=\"163\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/7/3372c1cb6d68cf97c2d231acc0b47b95a9ed04cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" />, being a length, must be positive, implying that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/9/9/49986ad1ae5d88da95d611165eb5055d9ffcaa25.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c=12$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"49\" height=\"12\" />. In fact, this is reasonable, since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/8/2/a821b1f9d0c53d73b5472e5488367d6912364387.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10+3\\approx 12$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"94\" height=\"15\" /> in the pentagon with apparently obtuse angles. Plugging this back into equations <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/d/9/0d9c3b1c142cbd3f8217dabc160c57e4750df241.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"21\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/2/f/62f62a19f0425d8e6121ca0c1cfd3ce96e43c9c5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(2)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"21\" height=\"18\" /> we find that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/8/b585e5c7f5850fdd752d075ff859b25432afbafe.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a = \\frac{44}{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"54\" height=\"37\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/8/c/18cb545dfde1f5bbeda99b1e0ccde882775506cd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b= \\frac{135}{10}=\\frac{27}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"108\" height=\"38\" />.\n</p><p>We desire <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/7/5/475db139d5cf51a72a2f5f3462f4041ad2166a92.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3c+a+b = 3\\cdot 12 + \\frac{44}{3} + \\frac{27}{2} = \\frac{216+88+81}{6}=\\frac{385}{6}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"422\" height=\"37\" />, so it follows that the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/4/d/b4de474c629d79eb01852c02dce57d26958f78d9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$385 + 6 = \\fbox{\\textbf{(D) }391}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"155\" height=\"28\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_3_.28Ptolemy.27s_but_Quicker.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3_(Ptolemy's_but_Quicker)\">Solution 3 (Ptolemy's but Quicker)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_24&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3 (Ptolemy&#39;s but Quicker)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let us set <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> to be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/7/7/3776ff652f06302eb25db2ffeb342544606414c9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AC=BD=CE$\" width=\"135\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> to be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/7/b/a7baf95ecafc2d7791788ec79aeeae390d60b119.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BE$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/3/b13f21416d84e13708696f34dea81026cda583c9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> to be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/5/bc56862b1fdb71204894da278e42ef75de73a40b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" />. It follow from applying <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Ptolemy%27s_Theorem\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Ptolemy&#39;s Theorem\">Ptolemy's Theorem</a> on <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/e/f9efaf9474c5658c4089523e2aff4e11488f8603.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABCD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"60\" height=\"14\" /> to get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/3/1/e315ade33e8d9bd19701767b48e95d7f0cfcaf16.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^2=9+10z$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"103\" height=\"18\" />. Applying Ptolemy's on <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/0/8/208eeb07928a5d764be9ca1d81d7a3f275308c65.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ACDE$\" width=\"57\" height=\"13\" /> gives <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/5/4/054aeba9c4a1075b14beb8a5a25fb5065eb5cde9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$xz=42+10x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"115\" height=\"15\" />; and applying Ptolemy's on <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/5/a/65af420a6e2b903f5295dd8f65f321545f69e44d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BCDE$\" width=\"58\" height=\"12\" /> gives <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/a/f5a6158d86c0ad80c376d318dbca542aae118631.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^2=100+3y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"112\" height=\"20\" />. So, we have the have the following system of equations:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/0/010c201b821bd29d55771ab1b99e2b14678efe32.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align} x^2 &amp;= 9+10z \\\\ x^2 &amp;= 100+3y \\\\ xz &amp;= 42+10x \\end{align}\" width=\"294\" height=\"72\" />\n</p><p>From <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/8/8/b88ea3916e8089c7edbccc3ff91e58e01a6e2682.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(3)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"21\" height=\"18\" />, we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7dcd03d2b1a1a0a4a71ac3dce92ba00f8e7dc98.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$42=(z-10)x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"118\" height=\"20\" />. Isolating the x gives <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/6/6/b661b965cb1e72a9dcd1365dcf30c742558239ab.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x=\\dfrac{42}{z-10}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -15px\" width=\"90\" height=\"40\" />. Plugging in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/6/6/b661b965cb1e72a9dcd1365dcf30c742558239ab.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x=\\dfrac{42}{z-10}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -15px\" width=\"90\" height=\"40\" /> to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/d/9/0d9c3b1c142cbd3f8217dabc160c57e4750df241.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"21\" height=\"18\" /> gives\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/c/6ccccffac16cb1821a5825c701ed47b2cb97f46b.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*} \\left(\\frac{42}{z-10}\\right)^2 &amp;= 10z+9\\\\ 10z^3 - 191z^2 + 820z + 900 &amp;= 1764\\\\ 10z^3 - 191z^2 + 820z - 864 &amp;= 0\\\\ (5z-8)(2z-27)(z-4) &amp;=0 \\end{align*}\" width=\"290\" height=\"125\" />\n</p><p>It is impossible for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/2/7/627b0e02cf5be1492969be616bf34707e0aa33d7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z&lt;10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"54\" height=\"15\" /> for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/d/6/cd6ee81a7a535d87853e848c77654cc36104a75e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x&lt;0$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"43\" height=\"13\" />; that means <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/f/5/1f5ca83bb8f455e3f5e81073031cf9e4e18b50e2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z=\\frac{27}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"57\" height=\"38\" />. That means <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/9/7/c975e64a5ed6e7d28e6f651e8102d070a417d4c2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x = 12$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"52\" height=\"12\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/2/5/b25cceee5bce459dd18f6b7121d8249fdbc36489.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y = \\frac{44}{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"58\" height=\"38\" />.\n</p><p>Thus, the sum of all diagonals is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/d/5/8d51fef71fd42da729cd4b54aa47290582d589ac.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3x+y+z = 3\\cdot 12 + \\frac{44}{3} + \\frac{27}{2} = 385/6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"308\" height=\"38\" />, which implies our answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/d/8/1d8fef4902a755aa198499b3864771be6420f240.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m+n = 385+6 = \\fbox{391 \\textbf{(D)}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"229\" height=\"30\" />.\n</p><p>~sml1809\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_4\">Solution 4</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_24&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 4\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<figure class=\"mw-halign-center\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:2014AMC12BProblem24Solution4.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/f/f1/2014AMC12BProblem24Solution4.png/400px-2014AMC12BProblem24Solution4.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"400\" height=\"400\" class=\"mw-file-element\" srcset=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/f/f1/2014AMC12BProblem24Solution4.png/600px-2014AMC12BProblem24Solution4.png 1.5x, https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/f/f1/2014AMC12BProblem24Solution4.png/800px-2014AMC12BProblem24Solution4.png 2x\" /></a><figcaption></figcaption></figure>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/d/2/bd2ca31d2ac24293f3593f24465bb5236b37fbdc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BE = a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"65\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/5/9/9590cb4591458ebe56fdcf5ae80fce4544287ad1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AC = CE = BD = b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"169\" height=\"14\" />\n</p><p>By <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Ptolemy%27s_theorem\" title=\"Ptolemy&#39;s theorem\">Ptolemy's theorem</a> for quadrilateral <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/4/9/249aa48167a0ec4808fb235a2796eaffab883dba.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABCE$\" width=\"56\" height=\"13\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/b/7/8b721c8f2bcef65614750d65f5df1cc5f7792612.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB \\cdot CE + BC \\cdot AE = BE \\cdot AC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"259\" height=\"16\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/c/9/0c9f007e3e81b05be65400d8c8f40f7cce25284c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3b + 140 = ab$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"110\" height=\"16\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/8/7/987eb4548c91b714dc95dea8d27bbbb4d5d7af10.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a = 3 + \\frac{140}{b}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"98\" height=\"38\" />\n</p><p>By <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Ptolemy%27s_theorem\" title=\"Ptolemy&#39;s theorem\">Ptolemy's theorem</a> for quadrilateral <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/5/a/65af420a6e2b903f5295dd8f65f321545f69e44d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BCDE$\" width=\"58\" height=\"12\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/3/a/d3a6c37b9ad5f51552f76bf9278812cd4b215080.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CD \\cdot BE + BC \\cdot DE = BD \\cdot CE$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"265\" height=\"16\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/b/2/fb2b0bb1ac7352dbfd80c75552eb1e422a9539d9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3a + 100 = b^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"110\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/6/a/a6a5dedfe0439505b414a66d34c28d5dd5654172.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3(3 + \\frac{140}{b}) + 100 = b^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"177\" height=\"38\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/a/6/1a63d3b2e17027e817115f8fdf81ec91d0a3090d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b^3 - 109 b -420 = 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"157\" height=\"18\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/0/e/d0ecf278f28298468918d8b28a8e8341fa165c4c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(b-12)(b+7)(b+5) = 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"204\" height=\"20\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/4/5/a450ff18c9509e2f70ba9f036b8ca9aeb33d49c7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b = 12$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"52\" height=\"14\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/a/9/0a9e0e005b8cf393cb826cde48de0a41a0c53fca.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a = 3 + \\frac{140}{12} = \\frac{44}{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"145\" height=\"38\" />\n</p><p>By <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Ptolemy%27s_theorem\" title=\"Ptolemy&#39;s theorem\">Ptolemy's theorem</a> for quadrilateral <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/2/4/124bf443dc6ea7c2746eb66958f1c1ec8fd845bc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABDE$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"60\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/8/8c821c7a6b40fc3525d4c3eb51579a0419faa808.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AE \\cdot BD + AB \\cdot DE = AD \\cdot BE$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"263\" height=\"16\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/c/f/ecf8146f92d131d3bc9dfa74d7aa65ec432c623a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AD \\cdot a = 14b + 30$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"144\" height=\"16\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/f/8/df8b2dc272721e2617f6b4808ae7b802380b2099.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AD = \\frac{27}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"77\" height=\"38\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/9/5/b953698a89461d32d51c13829648e443fbadcaf4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{m}{n} = 12 + 12 + 12 + \\frac{44}{3} + \\frac{27}{2} = \\frac{385}{6}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"289\" height=\"38\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/0/7/707a5d020355386cfe8e6d61d6e4fc1f35653134.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$385 + 6 = \\boxed{\\textbf{(D) }391}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"159\" height=\"30\" />\n</p><p>~<a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php/User:Isabelchen\">isabelchen</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_24&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"2\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_12B\" title=\"2014 AMC 12B\">2014 AMC 12B</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_12B_Problems\" title=\"2014 AMC 12B Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_12B_Answer_Key\" title=\"2014 AMC 12B Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/community/c13\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_23\" title=\"2014 AMC 12B